<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20595] lnetconfig: audit cYAML_get_object_item() callers for sibling-recursion matches</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20595</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;cYAML_get_object_item() searches recursively. It walks into the children of&lt;br/&gt;
the parent node, then into the parent's siblings through cy_next. A caller&lt;br/&gt;
that wants only a match under one parent can get a match from a later&lt;br/&gt;
sibling instead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20479" title="lnetctl: use-after-free in cYAML_build_error()" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20479"&gt;LU-20479&lt;/a&gt; fixed one instance of this shape in cYAML_build_error(). Gerrit&lt;br/&gt;
review on change 67235 found a second instance during the fix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;handle_yaml_config_ni() in lnet/utils/lnetconfig/liblnetconfig.c walks a&lt;br/&gt;
sequence of local NI entries:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  while (cYAML_get_next_seq_item(local_nis, &amp;amp;local_ni) != NULL) {&lt;br/&gt;
          intf = cYAML_get_object_item(local_ni, "interfaces");&lt;br/&gt;
          if (intf == NULL)&lt;br/&gt;
                  continue;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A parsed sequence item has cy_string set to NULL. When one local NI entry&lt;br/&gt;
has no "interfaces" key, the recursive search does not stop at that entry.&lt;br/&gt;
It falls through to the next sibling entry and returns that entry's&lt;br/&gt;
"interfaces" node instead. The "continue" statement only fires on the last&lt;br/&gt;
entry in the sequence, because only the last entry has no following&lt;br/&gt;
sibling to fall through to.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Audit the other cYAML_get_object_item() callers that predate commit&lt;br/&gt;
c906ab9c88ef ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-7734" title="LNet Multi-Rail Project" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-7734"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-7734&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; lnet: configuration fixes") for the same hazard.&lt;br/&gt;
For each caller, confirm the recursive search is safe in that context.&lt;br/&gt;
If it is not safe, replace the call with cYAML_get_object_child(), which&lt;br/&gt;
searches only the given parent's direct children.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
